\cf2 It is not that I disagree. But to be sure of our interpretation, we would need to take a good hard look at any counterevidence. Also, we still need to include both the broad sweep of Ezekiel's rhetoric in this chapter and specific rhetorical moves - if our interpretation is correct, it should explain both in detail, in ways that other interpretations do not. \
Our current hypothesis for the best interpretation is a layered one - a slight modification on what you proposed earlier, with a layer of land defiling sins interacting with expulsion from the land, a layer of royal failures, and a layer of practical atheism often manifesting in indifference at best to human life. \
These are the layers we need to connect properly to Ezekiel's rhetoric both in breadth and depth. These are the layers for which we want to find and examine counterevidence. We are not looking for evidence which doesn't fit a particular layer - as long as it fits at least one layer, that is consistent with the layered picture. We are looking for things which do not fit any layer, or otherwise call into question this particular layered approach.
